      "math_academy_id": "e-11025",
      "problem": "The function $f(x,y)$ is defined as \n\n$$\nf(x,y) = y^2 - \\log_3(x - 7).\n$$\n\nEvaluate this function at the point $(10,3).$",
      "worked_solution": "To evaluate our multivariable function at the point $(10,3),$ we substitute $x = 10$ and $y = 3$ into the function expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(10,3) & =({y}^{2}-{log}_{3}⁡(x-7)){|}_{(10,3)} \\\\  & ={3}^{2}-{log}_{3}⁡(10-7) \\\\  & =9-{log}_{3}⁡(3) \\\\  & =9-1 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(10,3)=8.$",
